      "point": "Both identify Atella as an ancient Italian town located between Capua and Nola.",
      "quote_britannica": "ATELLA, an ancient town of Gargania in Italy, between Capua and Nespolis.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "Atella was an ancient Oscan city of Campania, located 20km directly north of Naples."
    },
    {
      "point": "Both state that the ruins of Atella are still visible.",
      "quote_britannica": "The ruins of this town are full to be seen about 11 miles from the modern Averfa,",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The ruins of the city walls, private houses, the so-called garden of Virgil and many tombs remain,"
    },
    {
      "point": "Both connect Atella to the Atellan farce.",
      "quote_britannica": "From this town the Atlana fabule, or Atelani Inda, took their name.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The Atellan farce was one of the forms of entertainment of local origin that influenced the Latin theatre."
    },
    {
      "point": "Both mention that the modern town of Aversa was built from the materials of ancient Atella.",
      "quote_britannica": "which was built out of its materials.",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The diocese of Atella continued to exist until it became one of those incorporated into the new see of Aversa, which was founded in 1053."
    }
  ],
