    {
      "point": "Britannica claims the town's inhabitants were not deemed infamous and retained tribal rights, whereas Wikipedia does not mention this social status.",
      "quote_britannica": "The authors thank these forces were not reckoned among the common players, nor deemed infamous , but retained the rights of their tribe,",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The Atellan farce was one of the forms of entertainment of local origin that influenced the Latin theatre."
    },
    {
      "point": "Britannica places the ruins 11 miles from Aversa, while Wikipedia details the ruins across several comuni.",
      "quote_britannica": "The ruins of this town are full to be seen about 11 miles from the modern Averfa,",
      "quote_wikipedia": "The ruins of the city walls, private houses, the so-called garden of Virgil and many tombs remain, on sites in the comuni of Frattaminore, Orta di Atella, Sant'Arpino and Succivo,"
    },
    {
      "point": "Britannica includes a definition of 'tempo giusto' unrelated to Atella, while Wikipedia focuses entirely on the city's history.",
      "quote_britannica": "A TEMO GUISTO, in multic, figurities to flag or play in an equal, true, and just time.",
